{title: While It Is Day}
{subtitle: John 9:4}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 73}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
He passed by and saw a man
Blind from his [Eb]earliest [F]days
The dis[Eb]ciples stood and [Gm7]asked
Who sinned to [Eb]cause such pain [Fsus4]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Neither [Bb]this man nor his parents
Did sin [Eb]to bring this [F]state
It [Eb]happened so the works [Gm]of God
Might be re[Eb]vealed in his [Fsus4]fate
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]We must [Bb]do the works of him
Who sent me [Eb]while it is [F]day
Night is [Gm]coming when no one
Can work in [Eb]the fading light [Fsus4]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F]As long as [Bb]I am in the world
I am the [Eb]light of the [F]world
He [Eb]spat on the ground and [Gm]made
Mud with his [Eb]saliva [F]poured
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
We [Bb]must do the works of him
Who sent me [Eb]while it is [F]day
Night is [Gm]coming when no one
Can work in [Eb]the fading light [Fsus4]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[F]He [Eb]spread it on the man's eyes
And [Gm7]told him to go and wash
In the [Eb]pool of Si[Gm]loam
Which means the [Eb]one who was sent [Fsus4]
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]So the [Eb]man went and [Gm]washed
And came back [Eb]seeing the light [Fsus4][F]
[Bb]Work while it is day [Gm]
Before the [Eb]night ar[F]rives
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
